id: pm-graph-8z44
title: Enumerate minimal blocker frontiers for a goal with bounded completeness receipts
description: "Return alternative inclusion-minimal sets of unresolved blockers that intercept every upstream blocking path for a selected goal. Acceptance: brute-force small graphs validate cuts; cycles and unknown nodes are explicit; large graphs respect bounded search; typed SDK and CLI, compact agent output, actionable typed refusals, README/example, non-git real tracker validation. Overlap check: current core graph provides dominators, articulation, plan and impact; pm-graph provides path, critical-path and explain; pm-gantt-chart owns scheduling and slack; pm-context owns context projection; pm-web consumes graph data. Source inspection found no alternative minimal blocker frontier enumeration in these providers. Scope stays in pm-graph as graph-view-consumable data, with no duplication of traversal or scheduling commands."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T18:21:52.746Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T20:31:38.993Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T18:24:06.106Z",codex-agent,"Design: deterministic inclusion-minimal vertex separators over unresolved prerequisite paths, ordered by cardinality and id. All prerequisites are conjunctive; BLOCKS reverses orientation; hierarchy and RELATED are excluded. Frontier cuts unlock upstream plans, while immediatelyUnblocked reports direct eligibility; intermediate tasks still need completion. Full certified SDK reads retain terminal/external evidence. Goal-cone unknown nodes/statuses and cycles refuse with typed remedies. Separate graph/search receipts and hard input, work, state, size and output caps prevent false completeness. Validation: exhaustive small DAG oracle, non-git CLI with no git on PATH, bounded large graphs, behavioral revert, public tracker snapshot replay, unchanged npm/Bun gates."
  "2026-10-21T18:34:42.506Z",codex-agent,"Focused regressions: 11/11 pass, including independent brute-force oracle across all 1024 five-node DAGs, reversed BLOCKS, AND forks, different-sized alternatives, terminal boundaries, unknown-node/status receipts, cycle witnesses, every search budget and hard graph caps. Real CLI JSON/TOON and host row compaction pass in an initialized non-git tracker with an empty executable PATH and a Git discovery ceiling. Behavioral revert proof: disabling only cut emission inside minimalBlockerCuts makes all three selected oracle/chain/fork regressions fail (exit 1); original function restored. Lint, duplication (0 clones) and docstring checks pass. Dependency installation succeeded using a clean per-command npm user configuration; pins and lockfile unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T18:36:13.005Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public tracker replay: pm-graph origin/main f46704ef4083287ba54766a8a03e6e09df7ec7d6, independently verified public visibility and matching public main commit. Archived only tracked tracker files into a non-git scratch project; source records made read-only; replay ran with an empty executable PATH and Git discovery ceiling. Certified 99 items, projected 192 nodes/349 relationships, evaluated all 99 goals: 99 exhaustive searches, 0 refusals, 99 cuts including empty cuts; 1 goal had a nonempty frontier. Maximum 1 candidate state and 3 work units per goal; JSON result median 626 bytes/max 657; total replay 2391.77 ms on this run. Input records/settings/history fingerprint unchanged. This mostly terminal corpus validates real-data integration; exhaustive synthetic oracle and larger bounded cases validate alternatives and search limits."
  "2026-10-21T18:41:43.204Z",codex-agent,"CLI transport review: use the host-supported result exitCode contract for structured refusals so JSON/TOON retains graph receipts, cycle witnesses, unknown-id samples and remedies with nonzero status. Added real CLI cycle-receipt and bounded-search transport assertions. Search receipt proofs are independent of host row compaction. Read-only replay reports remain unchanged for the public snapshot. Local strict health reports inherited merge-fence drift and advisory stale items; merge-driver work remains explicitly out of scope."
  "2026-10-21T18:45:52.374Z",codex-agent,"Final CLI transport regressions pass: 11/11 focused tests. Returned-result refusals use the host exit_code field (distinct from thrown-error exitCode) and always include the declared cuts row collection. Real CLI confirms cycle witness/source certificate preservation at exit 2, unknown goal at exit 3, bounded partial search at exit 0, and row compaction receipts. The example is included in package files and package docs/examples metadata. No CLI/SDK defect remains from this feature validation."
  "2026-10-21T19:12:22.464Z",codex-agent,"Implementation committed as 097a772 and draft PR #154 opened for parallel CI validation. The CI workflow runs complete npm and Bun release gates on Node 26 and coverage on Node 22. Post-commit identity/privacy audit: 4/4 pass. Local isolated-identity npm gate remains in progress; one existing Neo4j query fast-failure test failed in the complete run and passes alone (1/1). Feature suite remains 11/11. No merge/release performed; draft status preserves the incomplete gate evidence."
  "2026-10-21T19:17:43.767Z",codex-agent,"CI at 097a772 completed 366/366 tests on both Node 22 and Node 26 with no skipped/canceled tests; Windows lifecycle also passed. Both Linux jobs correctly rejected aggregate line coverage 99.6697% below the unchanged 99.7% minimum (branches 95.59%, functions 100%). The only new missed lines are the replay script entry point; minimalBlockerCuts itself is 100/100/100. Exposed the replay main function, reused the shared entry guard, and added real entry-point success/missing-argument assertions with captured JSON receipts. No coverage threshold changed. The superseded slow local gate was stopped after its independently reproduced Neo4j timing failure; the isolated retry passed."
  "2026-10-21T19:27:09.091Z",codex-agent,"Verified implementation 6ecf09e: CI run 39660868399 passed Node 22 coverage (366/366), both npm run release:check and bun run release:check on Node 26 (366/366 each), and Windows lifecycle checks. No skipped/canceled package tests; thresholds unchanged. Aggregate coverage 99.74% lines, 95.59% branches, 100% functions; minimalBlockerCuts 100/100/100; duplication 0%. Latest linked pm test passed 11/11 with the replay entry-point assertions (86.243 seconds; execution timeout 300 seconds). Final read-only public snapshot replay at this implementation: 99 certified goals, 192 nodes/349 relationships, 99 exhaustive searches, 0 refusals, 99 cuts including empty cuts, 1 nonempty goal, maximum 1 state/3 work units, JSON median 626/max 657 bytes, 1441.54 ms; input fingerprints unchanged. Current core overlap was verified against installed/registry CLI 2026.10.21; pinned SDK 2026.10.15 retained. PR #154 remains unmerged and unreleased. Local caveats: inherited merge-fence drift, and a pre-existing Neo4j timing assertion that passed alone after failing under load; no pm CLI/SDK bug was found. Added durable acceptance receipts to the packaged worked example. Item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification; releasing the claim."
  "2026-10-21T20:27:44.332Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR #154: fetched every review thread with complete comments; two unresolved findings verified against the pinned SDK dependency-kind contract and command help. Latest CodeRabbit body has no outside-diff or nitpick findings. Plan: explicitly document all seven filter-capable commands; normalize BLOCKS for directional analytics while retaining stored graph/rendering endpoints; cover topo-sort, explain, path, critical chain, cycles, analyze and fallback impact with regressions and behavioral revert proofs. Branch contains current main. Run only targeted regressions, typecheck and lint locally, rebuild committed dist, and use CI npm/Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-21T20:30:54.031Z",codex-agent,"Verified regression failures with only the relevant behavior reverted, retaining the new tests: replacing only structuralEdges with its pre-review implementation makes node --test --test-name-pattern='BLOCKS analytics|mixed BLOCKS|real non-git' test/analytics-direction.test.ts fail 0/3 (all 3 failures, exit 1). Replacing only projectSubgraph makes node --test --test-name-pattern='BLOCKS analysis diagrams' test/analytics-direction.test.ts fail 0/1 (exit 1). Reverting only the README filter-support paragraph makes node --test --test-name-pattern='README filter support' test/analytics-direction.test.ts fail 0/1 (exit 1). Restored every change after each proof. Fixed file passes 5/5, including a real SDK-created non-git tracker exercising topo-sort, path in both directions, critical-path, explain and downstream impact. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint and committed-dist build pass on Node 26. Dependency install required a clean per-command npm user config due to inherited allow-scripts settings; no pin or lockfile changed."
  "2026-10-21T20:31:38.993Z",codex-agent,"Targeted validation through pm test --run --progress passed both linked commands: node --test test/blocker-cuts.test.ts test/blocker-cuts-command.test.ts (11/11), and node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/analytics-direction.test.ts test/analytics.test.ts (56/56). No failed, canceled, skipped or timed-out tests in this round. Full PR self-review checked orientation consumers and found additional affected diagram projections and analyze blocked-item counts, now fixed and covered. Stored graph relationships and default projectSubgraph key semantics remain intact. Rebuilt dist/index outputs; no coverage or duplication thresholds changed. Full release evidence is deferred to CI npm and Bun gates as requested."
